(vector (map (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:actor/wave 3), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:actor/scope-excluded-ops (vector :finalize-assembly-decision :finalize-assembly-operation :authorize-assembly-run :proceed-with-assembly-run :finalize-line-safety-clearance :declare-line-safety-cleared :declare-line-safe-for-operation :clear-line-for-operation :override-plant-safety-officer-judgment :override-safety-officer-judgment)), (:actor/robotics? true), (:adr/related (vector "adr-2607121000-cloud-itonami-global-isic-isco-reverse-toposort-plan" "adr-2799008122-cloud-itonami-isco-8122-metal-finishing-plating-coating-machine-operators-coverage")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "proceed with the assembly run" "proceed with the assembly operation" "authorize the assembly run" "authorize the assembly operation" "finalize the assembly decision" "finalize the assembly operation" "finalize the assembly-execution decision" "declare the line safety cleared" "declare the assembly line safety cleared" "declare the line safe for operation" "declare the assembly line safe for operation" "clear the line for operation" "clear the assembly line for operation" "finalize the line safety clearance" "finalize the line-safety clearance" "override the plant safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override plant safety officer judgment")), (:adr/id 2799008219), (:phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:log-work-record :flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order}, :auto #{:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation}}}"), (:actor/domain :manufacturing/assembly-line-scheduling-logistics-coordination), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :no-assembler :no-line :no-actuation :unknown-op :scope-excluded-action)), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:actor/isco-08 "8219"), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:adr/body "# ADR 2799008219: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 8219 Assemblers Not Elsewhere Classified line scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 8219\n-- Assemblers Not Elsewhere Classified** only. This is Wave3\n(production/trades); Wave0/1/2 are 100% complete, and Wave3 batches\n1-14 had already landed 84 occupations before this batch, leaving only\n17 gaps; this ADR completes the 82xx assemblers subgroup\n(`kotoba.occupation.wave/wave-of \"8219\"` resolves to wave 3).\n\n`gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8219` returned a clean\n404 before any work began -- this was a genuinely fresh scaffold, not\na resume of prior partial work.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"8219\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"8219\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Assemblers Not Elsewhere\nClassified\" -- confirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR\nthe entry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies\n[:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`.\nThis ADR and its companion registry edit promote the `8219` entry to\n`:implemented`.\n\n**Broad/generic assembly-line hazard dimension.** 8219 is a residual\n\"Not Elsewhere Classified\" ISCO-08 unit group covering diverse\nassembly-line work not captured by the more specific 8211 (Mechanical\nMachinery Assemblers) or 8212 (Electrical and Electronic Equipment\nAssemblers) unit groups. Standard assembly-line hazards apply\ngenerically here (pinch-point/crush hazard from moving parts and\nfixtures, hand-tool injury) without a single dominant hazard type,\nunlike e.g. 8122's narrow electroplating-chemical hazard. This actor\ndoes NOT model direct assembly-execution authority or line-safety-\nclearance authority. It is deliberately restricted to LINE SCHEDULING\nand LOGISTICS COORDINATION around the occupation (production-run/\ninventory/progress-record logging, crew/shift scheduling, safety-\nconcern escalation, and components/materials-stock procurement\ncoordination) -- never the assembly-execution decision or the\nline-safety-clearance decision itself, and never an override of a\nplant safety officer's judgment. The closed proposal-op allowlist\nstructurally excludes any op that could directly finalize such a\ndecision, and the governor independently, permanently hard-blocks any\nproposal whose rationale text names such a finalization action,\nregardless of the declared `:op` or confidence -- this is not an\nescalation path a human can approve through, it is an outright,\nstructural refusal at every maturity level.\n\nThe reference implementation named in this batch's task brief for\nmodule SHAPE was `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8211` (Mechanical\nMachinery Assemblers, a closely-related generic assembly-line safety\npattern) if already merged by a concurrent sibling agent; `gh api\nrepos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8211` returned a clean 404 at\nthe time this ADR was written (its registry entry was also still\n`:spec`), so this ADR falls back to the task brief's named alternate,\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8122`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8122)\n(Metal Finishing, Plating and Coating Machine Operators -- itself\nverified `:implemented` and independently re-cloned and read in full\nthis session). Its `platingcoord.{store,advisor,governor,actor}`\nmodule split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph shape, closed op-allowlist\n(identical four op names: `:log-work-record`, `:schedule-crew-\noperation`, `:flag-safety-concern`, `:coordinate-supply-order`) and\nscope-exclusion self-trip-guard design translate almost 1:1 onto this\noccupation's own generic assembly-line coordination scope, so this\nADR's `assemblycoord.*` modules follow the same shape with domain\nterms substituted (plater -> assembler, plating facility/plant ->\nassembly line/facility, plating-operation-execution ->\nassembly-execution, chemical-safety-clearance -> line-safety-\nclearance).\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8219` as an OSS\ndocumentation/logistics-coordination actor for assemblers not\nelsewhere classified, following the SAME governed-actor architecture\nas every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Assembly\nLine Scheduling Coordination Advisor ⊣ AssemblyCoordGovernor** on a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`,\ngit-sha-pinned identically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a\ndifferent library coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the\nunrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **line scheduling/logistics coordination\nONLY, never assembly-execution authority** -- it must NEVER be\ndesigned to exercise, simulate exercising, or propose exercising an\nassembly-execution decision or a line-safety-clearance decision.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- production-run/inventory/progress data\n  logging only\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/shift/task scheduling proposal\n  only\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a pinch-point/crush-hazard/hand-\n  tool-injury/equipment-condition concern, ALWAYS escalates\n  immediately, NEVER auto-commit-eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- components/materials-stock\n  procurement proposal only\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase,\nresembles an assembly-execution finalization decision or a\nline-safety-clearance finalization decision -- these are structurally\nabsent from the op-allowlist entirely, not merely gated behind\nescalation.\n\n### Five HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Assembler unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered assembler (crew member) record\n   (`:no-assembler`). Never trusts the proposal's own claim of who the\n   assembler is.\n2. **Line unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered assembly line/facility record\n   (`:no-line`).\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (`:no-actuation`; the governor never dispatches hardware\n   itself and never performs assembly work itself).\n4. **Op not allowed** -- any `:op` outside the closed four-op\n   allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`).\n5. **Scope-excluded action** -- the proposal's `:op` or `:rationale`\n   must never name an assembly-execution finalization, a\n   line-safety-clearance finalization, or a plant-safety-officer-\n   judgment override (`:scope-excluded-action`), REGARDLESS of the\n   declared `:op` or confidence. This is a hard, PERMANENT block --\n   there is no maturity level or confidence at which this actor may\n   auto-commit or human-approve its way past this rule; it is an\n   outright refusal, not an escalation.\n\n### Escalation gates (always human sign-off)\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's always-escalate path). The only channel by\n  which the robot may surface a pinch-point/crush-hazard/hand-tool-\n  injury/equipment-condition observation -- it never resolves the\n  concern itself.\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000) -- always needs human sign-off,\n  independent of confidence (boundary verified as exclusive by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`: exactly-at-threshold\n  commits, over-threshold escalates).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, CLAUDE.md)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as bare NOUNS (e.g.\n\"assembly\", \"component\", \"fixture\") can accidentally match inside the\nmock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- and generic assembly-line\nvocabulary is an especially sharp case of that risk, because routine\nwork-log/task text legitimately names assembly tasks, components and\nfixtures by name (e.g. a task literally described as \"routine assembly\ntask with pinch-point and hand-tool hazards near the component\nfixture\" -- hazard identification, not a proposal to finalize an\nassembly run or clear a line as safe). `assemblycoord.governor/scope-\nexcluded-phrases` is phrased exclusively as finalization ACTION\nPHRASES (\"proceed with the assembly run\", \"finalize the assembly\noperation\", \"declare the line safety cleared\", \"override the plant\nsafety officer's judgment\"), never bare nouns, and is checked only\nagainst the proposal's `:rationale` field (the advisor's own generated\ntext), never against raw `:task` input text.\n`assemblycoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-\nself-trip-on-scope-exclusion` is a dedicated regression test driving\nthe default mock-advisor across all four allowed ops with a task field\ncontaining exactly those bare domain nouns, asserting none of them\never hard-trip the finalization-scope rule. Green on first run.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"8219\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8219` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-8219`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary` immediately before the edit,\n  not assumed, to account for concurrent sibling landings in this same\n  batch -- the registry stood at `{:total 436, :spec 113, :blueprint\n  0, :implemented 323}` immediately before this batch began).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 31 tests, 67 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's `:test/\n  counts` and independently re-verified against a brand-new fresh\n  clone of the pushed repository (not just the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely\n  via the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent\n  with sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`) -- a single-entity EDN vector with an\n  `:adr/body` string blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n- This ADR completes the 82xx assemblers ISCO-08 subgroup\n  (8211/8212/8219) coverage for the ones landed as of this batch,\n  pending sibling agents' own landings for 8211/8212 in the same\n  batch.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-assembly-run`/`:approve-line-\n  safety-clearance` that is merely gated behind an always-escalate\n  path: rejected outright per the task's explicit guidance -- an\n  always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize an\n  assembly run or a line-safety clearance exists in the code path and\n  is merely deferred to a human gate. For a decision whose failure\n  mode is a pinch-point/crush injury or a hand-tool injury incident,\n  the capability itself must not exist in this actor at all.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"assembly\" \"component\"\n  \"fixture\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above -- this domain's own vocabulary necessarily\n  discusses assembly tasks, components and fixtures by name to do its\n  logging/scheduling job, so a bare-noun list would self-block the\n  actor's own legitimate proposals whenever a task description\n  mentions them.\n- Modeling a single dominant hazard type (as 8122's chemical-exposure\n  framing does): rejected -- 8219 is explicitly a residual NEC\n  category with no single dominant hazard, so `:hazard-type` on a\n  `:flag-safety-concern` proposal is kept as a free-form keyword\n  rather than a fixed enum, and the governor's always-escalate rule\n  for `:flag-safety-concern` does not branch on hazard-type value.\n- Mirroring `cloud-itonami-isco-8211` (the task brief's first-choice\n  reference) directly: not possible -- confirmed via `gh api` that\n  neither the repository nor an `:implemented` registry entry existed\n  for 8211 at the time this ADR was written, so the task brief's\n  documented fallback (`cloud-itonami-isco-8122`) was used instead.\n\n## Test verification\n\nFresh clone re-run immediately before writing this ADR:\n\n```text\nRunning tests in #{\"test\"}\n\nTesting assemblycoord.actor-test\n\nTesting assemblycoord.governor-test\n\nRan 31 tests containing 67 assertions.\n0 failures, 0 errors.\n```\n"), (:adr/date "2026-07-18"), (:test/counts "{:total 31, :assertions 67, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/name "Assemblers Not Elsewhere Classified Line Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice"), (:db/id -1), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :assembler-verification :line-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation :assembly-execution-line-safety-clearance-finalization-forbidden :plant-safety-officer-override-forbidden)), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-8219"), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8219"), (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8219)), (:test/simulator :assemblycoord.actor-test), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-8219 — Assemblers Not Elsewhere Classified Line Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000)), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-8219)))
